# Keep Guide.md updated

After any change to this portfolio (components, `content/site.ts`, `app/`, `lib/`, `public/` assets, scripts, config, or deploy setup), update `Guide.md` in the same turn before finishing.

- Treat `Guide.md` as the human-readable map of the repo, not optional extra docs.
- Update flowcharts, file tables (editable vs build), run/build/localhost steps, and Vercel steps when those facts change.
- If a file is added, removed, renamed, or its role changes, reflect that in the file map and architecture summary.
- If a feature, section, nav item, or content field is added, update the relevant “how it works” and “I want to change X” rows.
- Do not document `.next/`, `node_modules/`, or other generated output as source.
- Skip the Guide.md update only when the change is purely generated/cache output with no source or docs impact.
- When the change is user-visible (copy, layout, demos, or site chrome), also set `site.lastUpdated` in `content/site.ts` to today's date as Month Day, Year (for example `October 5, 2026`).
